<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Sandbox OFF for debug builds — global NSEvent monitors require no sandbox.
         Release/App Store builds use Halo.entitlements (sandboxed + XPC helper). -->
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <false/>

    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.downloads.read-write</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- App Group — REQUIRED for the widget to show anything, and it MUST be team-prefixed.
         `HaloWidget.appex` is sandboxed (WidgetKit requires it) and can only read the
         group container. The group is `R7S39UR27F.group.com.halo.mac`, NOT the iOS-style
         `group.com.halo.mac`. Measured 2026-10-25 on macOS 27.0.1 with probes signed exactly
         like the DMG (Apple Development certificate, no provisioning profile):

           group.com.halo.mac             unsandboxed writer -> second process reads nil
                                          (and a sandboxed reader gets nil: the widget is blind)
           R7S39UR27F.group.com.halo.mac   unsandboxed <-> sandboxed, both directions, share correctly

         On macOS 15+ an unprefixed group that is not authorised by a provisioning profile is
         access-controlled; the write is dropped without an error, so `UserDefaults(suiteName:)`
         still "works" inside one process while no other process ever sees it. `containerURL`
         even returns a path. The team prefix is what macOS trusts without a profile.

         History: this key was removed in 7f91bbb (2026-05-07) to stop a TCC prompt; restored
         for v2.3-beta.2 on the belief (gotcha 27, "verified 2026-09-12") that the unprefixed
         group works for an unsandboxed dev-signed app. It does not on current macOS, so the
         widget stayed blank through v2.4.0-beta.1. `scripts/audit-entitlements.sh` in its
         probe mode now proves sharing across real processes instead of trusting a string in a plist.

         Must equal `HaloWidgetData.suiteName` (Shared/HaloSharedData.swift) byte for byte. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>R7S39UR27F.group.com.halo.mac</string>
    </array>

    <!-- F-025: Similar Photos — optional Photos Library scan for near-duplicates.
         Entitlement + Info.plist NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription are wired, but the
         real permission-grant flow has NOT been runtime-tested this session. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.photos-library</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
